I have a binary version of PC-HACK that runs under MS-DOS available
for downloading on one of my FIDO systems.  The version is modified
to use ANSI cursor addressing, but will run under PC-DOS, using
ANSI.SYS.  It requires 256Kb memory, and does not include engravings.

The number for FIDO 109/483 (Wash-A-RUG FIDO) is 703-359-6179.

At 1200 Baud it will take about 41 minutes to download, using either
Xmodem, Modem7, or KERMIT.  Telelink takes about 31 minutes.  The HACK
files are in a .LBR library, so you will need a copy of the LU utility
to extract the files, which are squeezed, so (you guessed it) you also
need to have a copy of the USQ or NUSQ utility.  All of these are
available on this (and other) FIDO system.

